{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nNothing validates, before a reconcile pass mutates a live client Jira, that the mapped\nprojects actually EXIST / are visible to the bridge bot. Two live-only failure modes:\n1. A mapped-but-nonexistent (or decommissioned / permission-lost) project key is\n   syntactically valid, so `_validate_project_key` passes; the failure only surfaces\n   deep in fan-out as an ACLI error. This is exactly the `05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27` incident class.\n2. `resolve_project` (projects_store.py) returns `mapping.legacy_default` VERBATIM,\n   unvalidated. Every unbound/legacy ticket (absent bridge_project) resolves there. The\n   cross-project write guard's allowed set = `read_projects().keys()` and EXCLUDES creates\n   (applier.py `_cross_project_targets`), so a legacy_default pointing at a real-but-wrong\n   (or nonexistent) project drives a mass CREATE storm into the wrong place, unguarded.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a reconcile-pass PREFLIGHT that runs BEFORE any outbound mutation and validates that\nevery project in `read_projects(repo_root).keys()` PLUS `legacy_default` (when set) is\nvisible to the configured backend. The probe reuses `access_check.py`'s existing\n`AcliClient` transport and its retry helper (`_retry_sleep` / `JQL_RETRY_COUNT`): it calls\nthe client's ALREADY-PRESENT generic REST accessor `AcliClient._direct_rest_get`\n(acli_rest.py:207 — the same helper used by `get_issue_property`, `transition_issue`, and\n`validate_assignee_exists`) against `GET /rest/api/3/project/search` (paginated via\n`startAt`/`isLast`) to enumerate the bot-visible project keys. No new transport class or\nsubprocess is introduced — only a new `access_check.py` helper that consumes the existing\n`_direct_rest_get` accessor. On a missing/invisible project, FAIL FAST with a clear,\nactionable message naming the offending key(s) and the fix (correct projects.json /\nlegacy_default), rather than letting fan-out crash mid-pass. A hard auth/transport error\n(the probe cannot reach the backend) fails closed with its own distinct message, kept\nseparate from \"project not visible\". Wire it at the reconcile pass entry (`__main__.py`\n`run_pass_result`, strictly before `reconcile.reconcile_once`), skipping read-only passes\n(dry-run / reconcile-check / preview).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A pass with a mapped key not visible to the bot aborts at preflight with a clear\n      message naming the offending key BEFORE any Jira write (no call to\n      `reconcile.reconcile_once`). Verified by\n      `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_preflight_project_visibility.py -q`.\n- [ ] `legacy_default` (when non-empty) is included in the preflight visibility check and an\n      invisible `legacy_default` is caught, naming it. Verified by the same test module.\n- [ ] An all-visible mapping passes preflight and the pass proceeds unchanged\n      (`reconcile.reconcile_once` is called; no happy-path behavior change). Verified by the\n      same test module.\n- [ ] A hard auth/transport error fails closed with its own distinct message\n      (transport-unavailable, not project-not-visible) and the preflight is observable via a\n      log/stderr message. Verified by the same test module.\n\n## Testing\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_preflight_project_visibility.py -q` —\n  fake/injected transport (no live Jira): a fake client whose `_direct_rest_get` returns a\n  `project/search` page listing `{GOOD}` visible, `BAD` absent → preflight raises naming\n  `BAD` and the pass makes no mutation; an all-visible mapping passes and the pass proceeds;\n  `legacy_default=WRONG` (not visible) is caught; a `_direct_rest_get` that raises fails\n  closed with the transport-unavailable message. RED first: without the preflight the pass\n  proceeds to fan-out.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` from the worktree.\n\n## Sequencing\nLives in `access_check.py` (new mapped-projects preflight helper consuming the existing\n`_direct_rest_get` accessor) + wiring at the pass entrypoint (`__main__.py`\n`run_pass_result`). Disjoint from A/B/C/E files. Reads projects_store (no edit)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786809392434422001,"uuid":"dd77738b-2e9f-4f61-b627-e5b91d1de709"}